# Graphify: everything under graphify-out/ is generated, so none of it is
# tracked.  `graphify update .` rebuilds the lot from source in about five
# seconds with no API cost, and CLAUDE.md already asks for that after a code
# change, so there is nothing to commit and no rule to remember.
#
# Why not track any of it: the graph is an 11 MB JSON that every rebuild
# rewrites, and a git merge of it once produced 1,149 conflict markers that
# were committed, leaving `graphify query` unable to load it at all;
# manifest.json records file *mtimes*, so it differs on every machine and every
# fresh clone whatever the code does; the labels renumber their communities on
# every re-cluster; and the dated snapshots are a ~10 MB copy of the graph
# written per rebuild that nothing reads -- 14 of them were 81 % of this
# repository's entire object history.
#
# The one exception is .graphify_root, a one-byte marker that never changes.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/.graphify_root

# MacOS specific files
.DS_Store